      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Checkpoints per hour (whole cluster)",
      "description": "Timed checkpoints run on the schedule; requested ones are forced because WAL filled up between them. Requested checkpoints climbing means a write burst — on this cluster, most likely a graph-storage sync — is outrunning `max_wal_size`, and every forced checkpoint flushes shared buffers under load. Per instance, not per database.",
