    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Backend latency on the graph-storage routes",
      "description": "p50 and p95 of the backend's own request duration, per gear, for the gears that read and write graph-storage: domain-model, artifact-ingest and organizations, over 15 minutes. If these climb while the database panels above stay flat, the time is spent in the backend, not in Postgres. Gaps mean no requests to that gear in the window.",
